Let $m$ be the number of right angles in the octagon. Then we have $m$ angles equal to $90^\circ. $ We also have $m$ angles with measures at least $90^\circ$, and $8-m$ angles with measures at least $110^\circ$ by the $180^\circ$ angle sum property for polygons.

We need to find the maximum number of right angles. This will happen when the sided lengths of our $m$ and $8-m$ angles are all equal. To simplify our work, we use a chain of angle sum equalities:   \ begin{align*}
